:question/id #uuid "2f6ef83f-0afe-5013-adb1-85c6601a8666" :question/math-academy-id "q-115404" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $(4{x}^{6}+3)\\cdot (0.33)^{2x-5}\\ge 0.$" :question/worked-solution "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nDividing both sides of the given inequality by $(0.33)^{2x-5},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4{x}^{6}+3)\\cdot (0.33)^{2x-5} & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{(4{x}^{6}+3)\\cdot (0.33)^{2x-5}}{(0.33)^{2x-5}} & \\ge \\frac{0}{(0.33)^{2x-5}} \\\\ 4{x}^{6}+3 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFurthermore, $4{x}^{6}+3\\ge 0$ for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the solution is all real numbers." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115404/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f15241dd-898f-5f1c-9c1c-469a4af1fb80"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115404"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278181/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "be2c4390-5877-5cea-9688-e8e9af667086" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278181/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "19c93f1d-b187-54cc-abfd-f476ee8f7d58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278181/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6591f3ae-a7ff-541a-98a5-1e7aac725f23" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278181/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-278181/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-278181/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278181/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer/id #uuid "e89c13b1-c237-5019-95d5-e8b412f22da9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278181/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff80e483-9b77-55ce-9da3-e8d61e85fa89" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278181/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer-field/choices ["q-278181/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278181/field-3/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "64614e5a-5e27-5008-b241-bb1397ae8b29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278181/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "e57f2583-737d-559b-9560-9c15e2914f02" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278181/field-3/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-278181/field-3/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278181" :question/id #uuid "23c4ca3b-a23e-5058-8264-816d892804ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-278181" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $({x}^{2}-25)^{3}\\cdot {2}^{3x}<0.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n\n$<x$ \n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nDividing both sides of the given inequality by ${2}^{3x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-25)^{3}\\cdot {2}^{3x} & <0 \\\\ \\frac{({x}^{2}-25)^{3}\\cdot {2}^{3x}}{{2}^{3x}} & <\\frac{0}{{2}^{3x}} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-25)^{3} & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{({x}^{2}-25)^{3}} & <\\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ {x}^{2}-25 & <0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & <25 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{25} \\\\ |x| & <5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $-5<x<5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278181/field-1" "q-278181/field-2" "q-278181/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f15241dd-898f-5f1c-9c1c-469a4af1fb80"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278181"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115408/selection/bdfe48b0caad49e5bf0e0a6c20edb901c4411c09467480bd23a8ee01d956e72a" :answer/id #uuid "3da5bd22-6bdc-5fb9-8557-76136b98c398" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115408/selection/12cf5bf844cf95b95e80f529266ac6af4ed60a8ea790e2b44db6283719be635c" :answer/id #uuid "e6309cad-e51b-5ab6-b46b-f41107376365" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "all real numbers" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115408/selection/52f8bfd00f6b3deb0e93232df027641f8c16cee0e37ff5f896dd75bd009234e2" :answer/id #uuid "2136567f-782c-5036-8093-c4022d3e5876" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "no solutions" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115408/selection/0853a0542c597ebd74d0d7e25ff8e897f797a1258739f13a6eb1407ccb18bbd0" :answer/id #uuid "209aff17-19fb-5ad1-bcec-278429f58b3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115408/selection/484e812303ee353ae1663939df8cb7ca05a0e6231316bbff2ba5d3142f11caaf" :answer/id #uuid "81303778-c0bf-59b9-8ff9-75a5717f87a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3<x<2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115408/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "69595d5a-01f8-53b7-8e8d-77b5b4386bcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115408/selection/bdfe48b0caad49e5bf0e0a6c20edb901c4411c09467480bd23a8ee01d956e72a" :answer-field/choices ["q-115408/selection/bdfe48b0caad49e5bf0e0a6c20edb901c4411c09467480bd23a8ee01d956e72a" "q-115408/selection/12cf5bf844cf95b95e80f529266ac6af4ed60a8ea790e2b44db6283719be635c" "q-115408/selection/52f8bfd00f6b3deb0e93232df027641f8c16cee0e37ff5f896dd75bd009234e2" "q-115408/selection/0853a0542c597ebd74d0d7e25ff8e897f797a1258739f13a6eb1407ccb18bbd0" "q-115408/selection/484e812303ee353ae1663939df8cb7ca05a0e6231316bbff2ba5d3142f11caaf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115408" :question/id #uuid "94195579-c6ea-570a-b6e8-8733c4f53017" :question/math-academy-id "q-115408" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $(2x-5)^{3}\\cdot {3}^{x+6}<0.$" :question/worked-solution "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nDividing both sides of the given inequality by ${3}^{x+6},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x-5)^{3}\\cdot {3}^{x+6} & <0 \\\\ \\frac{(2x-5)^{3}\\cdot {3}^{x+6}}{{3}^{x+6}} & <\\frac{0}{{3}^{x+6}} \\\\ (2x-5)^{3} & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(2x-5)^{3}} & <\\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ 2x-5 & <0 \\\\ 2x & <5 \\\\ x & <\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115408/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f15241dd-898f-5f1c-9c1c-469a4af1fb80"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115408"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115410/selection/337f125045c7ba6decb19f15beb2d75c36b20dbb92f66de13ecb5eb225f58efa" :answer/id #uuid "46580a3e-f091-5d54-a45d-e2e6573aec63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115410/selection/c4d8fcc3d0001d305927fbe8d5a0bcc565b987d26bf192f936c7579b4dde886a" :answer/id #uuid "271a0841-346a-56be-8d84-3edc4cc0f80b