cdot {7}^{4x+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot {7}^{4x+2} & <-{x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{4x+1}+x\\cdot {7}^{4x+2} & <0 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{4x+1}+7x\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} & <0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+7x)\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} & <0 \\\\ x(x+7)\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${7}^{4x+1}$ and get\n\n$$\nx(x+7)<0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-7$ and $x=0.$ The parabola is below the $x$-axis when $-7<x<0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/b884ee15f864bcd02639085dc1465a82958ef0faeb9408e68b405c5906ea3a18.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-7<x<0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115458/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac76d62e-6bea-515a-af06-e4fae7bc1338"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115458"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278271/field-1/f022eff7ecaa4435243255d76a2a932e99db9e71ca2b89b05fafca75800709a0" :answer/id #uuid "7943d3f3-eb0c-5569-bff0-b8c289537e53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278271/field-1/22814de28a0b1b4f20d5edd62707d192b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa" :answer/id #uuid "5d1bdea7-a76b-565e-94fc-e9dfd0ec9090" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value ">" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278271/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2196882d-9dee-581e-9b76-fdff84b5f4ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278271/field-1/f022eff7ecaa4435243255d76a2a932e99db9e71ca2b89b05fafca75800709a0" :answer-field/choices ["q-278271/field-1/f022eff7ecaa4435243255d76a2a932e99db9e71ca2b89b05fafca75800709a0" "q-278271/field-1/22814de28a0b1b4f20d5edd62707d192b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278271/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "88d39343-fce0-5c73-ae07-10d4d3659f5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278271/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c954466-879d-5087-bbe2-5f59e286583c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278271/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-278271/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278271" :question/id #uuid "79b77f2e-0951-53fc-92e6-58cdcac40f68" :question/math-academy-id "q-278271" :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}\\le {4}^{4x+4}.$\n\n$x$ \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1} & \\le {4}^{4x+4} \\\\ {x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}-{4}^{4x+4} & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}-{4}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1} & \\le 0 \\\\ ({x}^{5}-{4}^{5})\\cdot {4}^{4x-1} & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${4}^{4x-1}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({x}^{5}-{4}^{5})\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}}{{4}^{4x-1}} & \\le \\frac{0}{{4}^{4x-1}} \\\\ ({x}^{5}-{4}^{5}) & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{5}-{4}^{5}) & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{5} & \\le {4}^{5} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{5}} & \\le \\sqrt[5]{{4}^{5}} \\\\ x & \\le 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality above is $x\\le 4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278271/field-1" "q-278271/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac76d62e-6bea-515a-af06-e4fae7bc1338"] :knowledge